WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.057 --> 00:00:04.158
Is your helmet on tight?

2
00:00:04.698 --> 00:00:05.819
Is your harness buckled?

3
00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:07.520
Are you feeling courageous?

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.401
Well then, let's fly!

5
00:00:12.403 --> 00:00:15.945
Today Josh and Anne are taking us on an adventure through the skies.

6
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:21.508
With no motor, no parachute, and no hot air balloon, they are going flying.

7
00:00:22.029 --> 00:00:23.750
How? With hang gliders!

8
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:29.798
Josh and Anne are joining us today in Queenstown, New Zealand, a city whose people are known for

9
00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:31.559
having fun in the great outdoors.

10
00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:36.563
"I have always wanted to fly, and I think hang gliding sounds like fun.

11
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:38.004
Do you want to come?"

12
00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:39.025
says Josh.

13
00:00:39.045 --> 00:00:42.768
"It sounds exciting, but I'm a little nervous about it.

14
00:00:43.228 --> 00:00:46.971
Then again, it's good to try new things so let's go!"

15
00:00:47.432 --> 00:00:47.972
says Anne.

16
00:00:49.173 --> 00:00:51.135
Hang gliding is actually very easy.

17
00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:54.637
Josh will fly with a championship glider named Tom.

18
00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.620
Tom is great at doing stunts and flying fast.

19
00:00:58.512 --> 00:01:02.693
Anne will fly with a glide instructor named Rick, who is good at teaching beginners.

20
00:01:05.714 --> 00:01:10.135
With the hang gliders packed on the roof of the van, everyone drives to the top of the

21
00:01:10.175 --> 00:01:11.916
mountain that overlooks Queenstown.

22
00:01:12.836 --> 00:01:17.758
It takes the instructors only twenty minutes to assemble poles and pieces into a complete glider.

23
00:01:18.218 --> 00:01:20.058
Josh and Anne seem pretty impressed.

24
00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:24.940
Rick calls Anne over for her first lesson on flying.

25
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.566
"Okay, first, you need a helmet that fits your head well.

26
00:01:29.066 --> 00:01:30.127
How does this one work?"

27
00:01:30.147 --> 00:01:35.051
"It feels comfortable and nice and hard," says Anne.

28
00:01:35.991 --> 00:01:38.233
Then Rick explains the next piece of equipment.

29
00:01:38.253 --> 00:01:40.755
"Great. Next you need a harness.

30
00:01:41.315 --> 00:01:42.356
This one should fit you.

31
00:01:42.897 --> 00:01:45.939
It looks like a sleeping bag, but it is very strong.

32
00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:49.562
It will hook you to the glider tightly so you can't fall out."

33
00:01:49.582 --> 00:01:52.404
"I'd better not fall out!"

34
00:01:54.504 --> 00:01:58.846
While Rick and Anne get her harness fitted, Tom gets Josh ready for their jump.

35
00:01:59.207 --> 00:01:59.947
"Cheers, Josh.

36
00:02:00.187 --> 00:02:03.229
When we're hooked up to the glider, I'll ask if you're ready.

37
00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:06.951
If you feel nervous and you're not ready, say 'Wait.'

38
00:02:07.411 --> 00:02:09.172
But, if you feel ready, say 'Ready.'

39
00:02:09.632 --> 00:02:09.952
Got it?"

40
00:02:10.733 --> 00:02:13.114
"Excellent! I'm ready to fly already!

41
00:02:13.394 --> 00:02:13.995
Let's go!"

42
00:02:14.455 --> 00:02:15.055
says Josh.

43
00:02:15.755 --> 00:02:18.937
"In just a minute, we'll start back here, away from the edge.

44
00:02:19.457 --> 00:02:22.899
When you say ready, I'll count one, two, three.

45
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.005
At one, we start running.

46
00:02:25.585 --> 00:02:26.806
At two, we run harder.

47
00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.488
At three, we throw ourselves off the cliff."

48
00:02:29.508 --> 00:02:31.950
"I throw myself off the cliff?"

49
00:02:32.471 --> 00:02:33.472
Josh is worried.

50
00:02:34.232 --> 00:02:36.074
"Don't worry," explains Tom.

51
00:02:36.554 --> 00:02:37.895
"Your wings will be attached.

52
00:02:38.456 --> 00:02:42.279
It's important that you run faster and faster as I count from one to three.

53
00:02:42.839 --> 00:02:47.623
When we run fast off the edge, it gives our glider momentum and pushes us out.

54
00:02:48.143 --> 00:02:50.986
But if we go slowly, we'll fall straight down.

55
00:02:51.326 --> 00:02:51.646
Got it?"

56
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:52.687
"I got it.

57
00:02:53.227 --> 00:02:53.788
No worries."

58
00:02:55.656 --> 00:02:57.937
Running in a harness is more difficult than it looks.

59
00:02:58.437 --> 00:03:00.878
It's like running with a sleeping bag around your legs.

60
00:03:01.398 --> 00:03:04.939
While Josh practices running, Rick teaches Anne how to steer.

61
00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:07.859
"Turning the glider is really simple, Anne.

62
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.461
There is a triangular bar in front that is attached to the top of the glider.

63
00:03:12.981 --> 00:03:15.882
If we want to go left, we push the bar to the right.

64
00:03:16.402 --> 00:03:19.123
If we want to go up, we push the bar forward.

65
00:03:19.703 --> 00:03:21.983
And pulling the bar towards us sends us down.

66
00:03:22.444 --> 00:03:23.804
But I don't recommend that."

67
00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.163
"I think I'll let you do the steering, thanks," says Anne.

68
00:03:29.124 --> 00:03:32.947
Once everyone has practiced, it's time to get strapped into the gliders.

69
00:03:33.628 --> 00:03:38.992
Anne reminds herself it's good to try new things, and Josh reminds himself of the one-two-three.

70
00:03:39.913 --> 00:03:41.214
Josh and Tom go first.

71
00:03:41.774 --> 00:03:42.995
"Ready?" "Ready!"

72
00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:47.980
"One two three And they're off!

73
00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:53.044
Anne and Rick are up next, and soon they are flying right above Josh and Tom.

74
00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:58.087
While Josh and Tom are diving and flying sideways, Anne and Rick take in the view.

75
00:03:58.768 --> 00:04:03.931
Hang gliding is a nature-friendly sport because there is no noise and no pollution.

76
00:04:04.652 --> 00:04:06.553
Both gliders circle the fields below.

77
00:04:07.093 --> 00:04:08.314
And it's a perfect landing!

78
00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:12.117
"That was the most beautiful flight I could have imagined!

79
00:04:12.657 --> 00:04:16.480
It was so peaceful, I actually felt natural up there!"

80
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.420
says Anne.

81
00:04:17.941 --> 00:04:20.943
Josh agrees, but with a different sort of enthusiasm.

82
00:04:20.963 --> 00:04:23.757
"Woo-hoo! That was amazing!

83
00:04:24.238 --> 00:04:27.480
We flew sideways and did all sorts of dives and turns.

84
00:04:28.021 --> 00:04:29.742
It was absolutely awesome.

85
00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.685
Wow! I can't wait to do that again."

86
00:04:33.245 --> 00:04:37.269
This concludes another short but thrilling adventure with Josh and Anne.

87
00:04:37.749 --> 00:04:40.191
Who knows where their next adventure may take us!

88
00:04:40.551 --> 00:04:40.872
Bye!
